Arch tips:

1) Get some armor - pronto. Mithril is a good bet, and the mines are a
logical place for an Arch to be mucking around.

2) Pets are massively helpful to an archaeologist, I've found. Tame
every dog, cat and horse you find. Any you can't tame, pacify.

3) Don't bother advancing bullwhip skill - a bullwhip is almost
useless against a "thick-skinned" monster. Switch to pick-axe
immediately and never look back.

4) Don't forget you can scribble Elbereth in the dust; use it early
and often. Find a decent means of engraving/burning to save your
bacon, if possible.

5) Work your way to Minetown, preferably with several pets. Sell some
gems to get cash, buy some protection, and get yourself armored.

6) Tin dangerous (e.g. poisonous) corpses before eating them. Bless
that tinning kit if you get a chance.

7) Use (or abuse) every trick in the book.

Good luck!

